type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\vec{v}\\ne\\vec{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755599} {:answer/feedback "This is the defining relation, with the additional requirement that $\\vec v\\ne\\vec0$." :answer/id #uuid "e29c04ba-aa12-5636-be57-0f48f1ac8744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\vec{v}=\\lambda\\vec{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755612} {:answer/feedback "Eigenvectors are required to be nonzero. The zero vector satisfies the equation for every scalar and therefore cannot identify an eigenvalue." :answer/id #uuid "ea1f6d2c-4370-556f-a1ed-b18cdbb2acd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\vec{v}$ is the zero vector" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755614}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755612} :answer-field/id #uuid "fba20990-bcb2-58c5-9803-6761594d97ec" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755616}] [:answer/id #uuid "93bfb916-fe8e-5d2a-aba2-f52d9a3e8f69" {:answer/feedback "If $A$ is $m\\times n$, then $\\vec v$ has $n$ components and $A\\vec v$ has $m$; equality with $\\lambda\\vec v$ requires $m=n$." :answer/id #uuid "93bfb916-fe8e-5d2a-aba2-f52d9a3e8f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Yes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755604}] [:answer/id #uuid "e29c04ba-aa12-5636-be57-0f48f1ac8744" {:answer/feedback "This is the defining relation, with the additional requirement that $\\vec v\\ne\\vec0$." :answer/id #uuid "e29c04ba-aa12-5636-be57-0f48f1ac8744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\vec{v}=\\lambda\\vec{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755612}] [:answer/id #uuid "e463c948-a56b-5dd3-b3fa-46a3203c99db" {:answer/feedback "The equality supplies the needed dimensional information: $A\\vec v$ and $\\lambda\\vec v$ must have the same number of components." :answer/id #uuid "e463c948-a56b-5dd3-b3fa-46a3203c99db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No